course: dictionary
lesson: 11786
title: Words that change meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. Beige is a colour name, but people also use it as slang. «Her new school coat is beige.» Here beige is a colour: a pale, light brown, like sand.
explain: Now look at this sentence: «The film was so beige, I fell asleep halfway through.» A film cannot be a colour, so the word must mean something else. The clues are fell asleep and so, which tell you the film was dull. Here beige means boring.
explain: Ask yourself which meaning fits the sentence. Try the colour meaning first. If it makes no sense, try the other meaning. The context clues decide which meaning the word has.
fact: Beige is a pale, light brown colour, like sand or milky tea.
fact: In art lessons, beige is a neutral colour, made by mixing white with a little brown or yellow.
fact: Many walls, carpets, coats and school uniforms are beige.
fact: As slang, «beige» means dull or boring, with nothing exciting about it.
exercise: «Her new school coat is beige.» What colour is beige here? | A bright green, like fresh grass | A bright red, like a fire engine | *A pale, light brown, like sand | A deep blue, like the sea
exercise: «The film was so beige, I fell asleep halfway through.» What does beige mean here? | *Dull and boring | Bright and exciting | Pale and cold | Very wet
exercise: Why can beige not be a colour in «The film was so beige»? | Films are always beige | *A film is not a colour, and fell asleep shows the film was dull | The word beige is always a colour | Because the sentence has the word so in it
test: «The walls of the hall were painted beige.» What colour are the walls? | *Pale, light brown | Sky blue | Bright purple | Jet black
test: «Her outfit was so beige that nobody remembered it.» What does beige mean? | *Dull and plain | Shiny and new | Bright and colourful | Pale brown
exam: «The beige sofa matches the carpet.» In this sentence, what is beige? | *A colour | Something boring | A type of food | A kind of noise
